# Signers of BQCA live capture receipts (#559), in the OpenSSH allowed signers
# format (see "ALLOWED SIGNERS" in ssh-keygen(1)).
#
# tools/finalize_live_sync.py records a live template verification in
# bindings/bqca_report_template.yaml only with a capture receipt that
# `ssh-keygen -Y verify` verifies against this file, in the
# `bqca-live-capture-receipt` namespace, for the receipt's `signer`.
# tools/sign_live_capture.py signs such receipts. Each line lists one signer:
#
#   <signer> namespaces="bqca-live-capture-receipt" <key type> <public key>
#
# where <signer> is the public name that receipts and the binding give for a
# maintainer who exports the live template with the internal report tooling
# (for example a GitHub username: letters, digits, '.', '_', '@', '+' or '-'),
# and the key is that maintainer's SSH public key. A line is added, changed
# or removed only in a reviewed change. No signer is listed yet, so no
# receipt is trusted and no write can finalize the binding.
